# Assets Module

## Purpose

Data-driven asset loading pipeline. `ImageLoader` reads image files from disk. `AnimationClip` loads animtool frame-sequence exports as bindless textures. `SceneResourceLoader` parses a scene manifest and dispatches each section to a registered `Delegate`.

`assets` must not depend on `ecs` or `ui`. Loading implementations live in the modules that own the target subsystems (`core/ecs/loaders/`, `core/ui/`).

## Static Sprites vs Animation

| Use case | Asset format | Loading path |
|---|---|---|
| **Static sprites** (ship, asteroid, background) | Standalone PNG per sprite | Declared in scene manifest -> `SceneResourceLoader::GetTexture( path )` |
| **Animated sprites** (bullets, FX) | animtool `animation.json` + per-frame PNGs | Declared in scene manifest -> `SceneResourceLoader::GetClip( path )` |
| **Sounds** | WAV/MP3 | Declared in scene manifest -> `SceneResourceLoader::GetSound( path )` |
| **Fonts** | TTF | Declared in scene manifest `fonts` section; loaded via `FontLoadDelegate` (no getter) |

## Key Classes

| Class | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| `ImageLoader` | Wraps STB image; loads PNG/JPEG/BMP into a raw `Image` struct |
| `ImageLoader::Image` | POD: `data` (raw bytes), `width`, `height`, `num_channels` |
| `AnimationClip` | Loads animtool JSON; registers frame PNGs bindless; stores ordered `Frame` array |
| `AnimationClip::Frame` | `texture_index`, `duration_sec` |
| `SceneResourceLoader` | Manifest dispatcher + opaque path-to-id catalog facade |
| `SceneResourceLoader::Delegate` | Loads one named section; lives in the owning module |

## Scene Manifest

**File:** `resources/scenes/<scene_name>.json`

```json
{
  "textures": [
    "./resources/textures/ship/Ship.png"
  ],
  "animations": [
    "./resources/textures/bullets/anim_defaultBullet/animation.json"
  ],
  "sounds": [
    { "path": "./resources/sounds/laser.wav", "pool_size": 4, "looping": false }
  ],
  "fonts": [
    "./resources/font/OpenSans-Regular.ttf"
  ]
}
```

- **Path is the ID:** lookup strings must match manifest entries exactly (including `./resources/...` prefix).
- **Frame PNGs** for animation clips are loaded inside `AnimationClip::Load` -- do not list them in `textures`.
- **Materials/meshes** are not in the manifest; create them in code via `RenderSystem`.
- **Unknown sections** are logged when no delegate is registered for that key.

## API

```cpp
// Shell (VortexGame::Init) -- register delegates once
loader.RegisterDelegate( TextureLoadDelegate::SECTION_KEY, texture_delegate );
loader.RegisterDelegate( FontLoadDelegate::SECTION_KEY, font_delegate );

// Scene enter -- LoadManifest BEFORE UIView::LoadDocument (fonts needed at parse time)
resource_loader.LoadManifest( "./resources/scenes/main_scene.json" );

// Gameplay lookup by path
uint32_t tex = resource_loader.GetTexture( "./resources/textures/ship/Ship.png" );
uint32_t clip_id = resource_loader.GetClip( "./resources/textures/bullets/anim_defaultBullet/animation.json" );
uint32_t sound_id = resource_loader.GetSound( "./resources/sounds/laser.wav" );
```

Delegates (`TextureLoadDelegate`, `AnimationLoadDelegate`, `AudioLoadDelegate`, `FontLoadDelegate`) own the actual load calls. Game code should prefer manifest + lookup.

## JSON Format (animtool export)

**AnimationClip** (`animation.json`):
```json
{
  "flip": false,
  "frames": [
    { "texture": "frame_000.png", "duration_ms": 50 },
    { "texture": "frame_001.png", "duration_ms": 50 }
  ]
}
```

Frame PNG paths are resolved relative to the JSON file directory.

## Key Patterns

- **Load once, share:** manifest preload + per-system caches; many entities reference the same handles.
- **Delegate registry:** shell owns delegates and registers them; scenes only call `LoadManifest`.
- **Catalog facade:** getters stay on `SceneResourceLoader`; section tables are opaque `uint32_t` ids.
- **Bindless frames:** Each frame is a separate PNG in the bindless texture array -- no atlas UV math.
- **Default fallback:** `GetFrame()` returns a default frame if index is out of range.
- **STB ownership:** `Image::data` is heap-allocated by STB. Lifetime matches the `Image` struct.

## DOs

- Declare all scene file-backed assets in the scene manifest JSON
- Use `SceneResourceLoader::Get*` with the exact path from the manifest
- Add new asset types by implementing `Delegate` in the owning module and registering it in the shell
- Call `LoadManifest` before any consumer that needs those assets (especially RmlUi documents)

## DON'Ts

- Don't make `core/assets` depend on `ecs` or `ui`
- Don't scatter `CreateTexture` / `LoadClip` / `LoadSound` / `LoadFontFace` calls with hardcoded paths in gameplay systems
- Don't store `Image::data` pointer beyond the `Image` struct lifetime
- Don't list animation frame PNGs separately in the manifest `textures` array
